{"name":"Parisian Café","hex":"#978478","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"café","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A coffee shop; an establishment selling coffee and sometimes other non-alcoholic beverages, simple meals or snacks, with a facility to consume them on the premises.","A small restaurant of any genre."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caf%C3%A9"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parisian café","blocks":[{"text":"A Parisian café is a type of café found mainly in Paris, where in addition to serving food and drink it can serve as a meeting place, neighborhood hub, and place to relax in a congenial atmosphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Caf%C3%A9_de_la_Paix_Paris_France.JPG/330px-Caf%C3%A9_de_la_Paix_Paris_France.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parisian_caf%C3%A9","wikidata":"Q7137468"},{"title":"Coffeehouse","blocks":[{"text":"A coffeehouse, coffee shop, or café, is an establishment that serves various types of coffee drinks like espresso, latte, americano, and cappuccino, as well as other beverages. An espresso bar specializes in serving espresso and espresso-based drinks. Some coffeehouses may serve iced coffee among other cold drinks, as well as non-caffeinated drinks. A coffeehouse may also serve food, such as light snacks, sandwiches, muffins, cakes, breads, pastries, or doughnuts. Many doughnut shops in Canada and the US serve coffee to accompany doughnuts, so these can also be classified as coffee shops, although doughnut shops tend to be more casual and serve cheaper fare. In continental Europe, some cafés even serve alcoholic drinks, and in West Asia, coffeehouses may offer a flavored tobacco smoked through a hookah, called shisha in most varieties of Arabic or nargile in Levantine Arabic, Greek, and Turkish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Caf%C3%A9_de_Flore.jpg/330px-Caf%C3%A9_de_Flore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffeehouse","wikidata":"Q30022"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Au_Vieux_Paris_d%27Arcole%2C_1_May_2018.jpg/500px-Au_Vieux_Paris_d%27Arcole%2C_1_May_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Au_Vieux_Paris_d%27Arcole%2C_1_May_2018.jpg/1280px-Au_Vieux_Paris_d%27Arcole%2C_1_May_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Au_Vieux_Paris_d%27Arcole%2C_1_May_2018.jpg/500px-Au_Vieux_Paris_d%27Arcole%2C_1_May_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ornate exterior of the Au Vieux Paris d'Arcole, a Parisian café dating from 1512","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAu_Vieux_Paris_d'Arcole%2C_1_May_2018.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Paris_-_36_Cour_Saint-%C3%89milion_-_20111107_%281%29.jpg/500px-Paris_-_36_Cour_Saint-%C3%89milion_-_20111107_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Paris_-_36_Cour_Saint-%C3%89milion_-_20111107_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Paris_-_36_Cour_Saint-%C3%89milion_-_20111107_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Paris_-_36_Cour_Saint-%C3%89milion_-_20111107_%281%29.jpg/500px-Paris_-_36_Cour_Saint-%C3%89milion_-_20111107_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" The terrace of the \"Partie de Campagne\" tea room at the Saint-Émilion courtyard in Bercy Village","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParis_-_36_Cou